```

---

### How to add them

Just open your `.gitignore` file in VSCode and add the lines at the bottom. Then save with **Ctrl+S**.

---

### But think about which ones you actually want to ignore
```
test_api.py      → useful for teammates to test, KEEP it in git ✅
debug_test.py    → development only, ignore it ❌
encode_img.py    → one-off script, ignore it ❌
download.jpg     → test image, ignore it ❌
*.jpg / *.png    → careful with this — it ignores ALL images
                   including any you might want to keep